      "updated": 1781019622804,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n1) Functional Requirements:  \n- User should be able to stream and share videos\n- Content team/users should be able to upload new videos\n- User should be able to search for videos using titles or tags\n- System must support content geo-blocking\n- System must support board story (hover preview image on video\npointer)\n- User should be able to pause and resume video playback from left-off\npointh\n\n---- Out of scope ------\n- recommendation engine and discover weekly generation.\n- protection against copyrighted or bad content.\n\n2) Scale of the System: \n- Total Users: 1 Billion\n- Daily Active Users (DAU): 200 Million\n- Views: 1 Billion videos watched per day (avg 5 videos/user/day)\n- Uploads: Assumed 10 Million videos uploaded per day (based on 100:1\nread/write ratio)\n- Average video size: 100 MB\n\n3) Non Functional Requirements (SPARCS):  \n- Scalability: System must handle 1B streams/day and immense global\nconcurrent traffic.\n- Performance: Low latency streaming with fast playback start times;\nminimal rebuffering.\n- Availability: Highly available architecture via CDNs to stream video\nglobally without disruption.\n- Reliability: High reliability (no lost uploads), Adaptive quality switching\n\n4) BOE Calculations: \n- Load / Traffic (QPS)\n    > Read QPS: (1B)/ (10^5) => 10k QPS\n    > Write QPS: 10M/(10^5) = 100 QPS\n    > Peak QPS: (X3) ≈ 30k QPS\n\n- Storage\n    > Daily storage = 10M writes × 100MB average request => 1 PB\n    > Yearly storage = 1PB × 365 => 365 PB\n    > Total storage = 365*10 => 3650PB\n    > replication ≈ 3650*3 = 10,950PB  \n\n- Bandwidth\n    > Ingress = 100 QPS × 100 MB => 10 GB/s\n    > Egress = 10,000 QPS × 100 MB => 1 TB/s\n\n- Cache \n    > 1B × 100 MB × 0.20 => 20 PB\n\n5) Core Entities \n- User\n- Videos\n- Tags\n- Views\n\n6) API Design \n\nGET /videos\n    Input: {searchQuery, tags}\n    Output: [{videoMetadata}]\n\nPOST /videos\n    Input: {videoMetadata, videoFile}\n    Output: 2xx, success\n\nGET /videos/{videoId}/play\n    Input: {videoId, auth_token}\n    Output: {videoStream}\n\nPOST /users/{userId}/history\n    Input: {videoId, timestamp_left_off}\n    Output: 2xx, success\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n1) Functional Requirements:  \n- User should be able to stream and share videos\n- Content team/users should be able to upload new videos\n- User should be able to search for videos using titles or tags\n- System must support content geo-blocking\n- System must support board story (hover preview image on video pointer)\n- User should be able to pause and resume video playback from left-off pointh\n\n---- Out of scope ------\n- recommendation engine and discover weekly generation.\n- protection against copyrighted or bad content.\n\n2) Scale of the System: \n- Total Users: 1 Billion\n- Daily Active Users (DAU): 200 Million\n- Views: 1 Billion videos watched per day (avg 5 videos/user/day)\n- Uploads: Assumed 10 Million videos uploaded per day (based on 100:1 read/write ratio)\n- Average video size: 100 MB\n\n3) Non Functional Requirements (SPARCS):  \n- Scalability: System must handle 1B streams/day and immense global concurrent traffic.\n- Performance: Low latency streaming with fast playback start times; minimal rebuffering.\n- Availability: Highly available architecture via CDNs to stream video globally without disruption.\n- Reliability: High reliability (no lost uploads), Adaptive quality switching\n\n4) BOE Calculations: \n- Load / Traffic (QPS)\n    > Read QPS: (1B)/ (10^5) => 10k QPS\n    > Write QPS: 10M/(10^5) = 100 QPS\n    > Peak QPS: (X3) ≈ 30k QPS\n\n- Storage\n    > Daily storage = 10M writes × 100MB average request => 1 PB\n    > Yearly storage = 1PB × 365 => 365 PB\n    > Total storage = 365*10 => 3650PB\n    > replication ≈ 3650*3 = 10,950PB  \n\n- Bandwidth\n    > Ingress = 100 QPS × 100 MB => 10 GB/s\n    > Egress = 10,000 QPS × 100 MB => 1 TB/s\n\n- Cache \n    > 1B × 100 MB × 0.20 => 20 PB\n\n5) Core Entities \n- User\n- Videos\n- Tags\n- Views\n\n6) API Design \n\nGET /videos\n    Input: {searchQuery, tags}\n    Output: [{videoMetadata}]\n\nPOST /videos\n    Input: {videoMetadata, videoFile}\n    Output: 2xx, success\n\nGET /videos/{videoId}/play\n    Input: {videoId, auth_token}\n    Output: {videoStream}\n\nPOST /users/{userId}/history\n    Input: {videoId, timestamp_left_off}\n    Output: 2xx, success\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
