      "updated": 1781028281115,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) Messaging\n- Client Send: User sends message; client emits send_message via WebSocket\n(includes chat_id, content, optional parent_message_id).\n- Gateway: Authenticates session, checks rate limits, and routes to correct -\nChat Server using consistent hashing.\n- Validation & Storage: Chat Server verifies user in chat_members. Generates\nmessage_id, timestamp, and saves to messages table.\n- Fan-out: Chat Server finds active DeviceSessions and broadcasts\nnew_message to online participants.\n\n2) Rich Media Support (Images/Video)\n- Decoupled Upload: Media is never sent over WebSockets to prevent blocking\ntext messages.\n- Object Storage: Client uploads file directly to an Object Store (e.g., S3) via\nHTTP REST API.\n- Message Attachment: Client receives a media_url from S3 and attaches it\nto the standard WebSocket payload.\n\n3) Real-Time Notifications (Online vs. Offline)\n- Presence Check: Chat Server checks device_sessions to split participants\ninto Online and Offline buckets.\n- Online Routing: Broadcasts instantly via WebSocket.\n- Offline Routing: Writes message to inbox table and triggers FCM/APNs push\nnotification.\n- Reconnect Replay: When an offline user opens the app, Gateway connects\nWS, fetches missed messages from inbox, and marks delivered_at.\n- Cleanup: Background cron job purges undelivered inbox messages after 30\ndays.\n\n4) Message Deletion\n- Client Request: Client emits delete_message WebSocket event with\nmessage_id.\n- Authorization: Chat Server verifies the requester is the original sender_id.\n- Soft Delete: Server updates messages table, setting is_deleted = true\n(never hard delete).\n- Online Sync: Server broadcasts message_deleted event to instantly update\nactive UIs.\n- Offline Sync (Delivered): Queues deletion event in inbox for devices that\nalready received the text.\n- Offline Sync (Undelivered): Silently removes the inbox row. Recipient never\nsees the original message or the deletion event.",
      "fontSize": 20.273538308073675,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) Messaging\n- Client Send: User sends message; client emits send_message via WebSocket (includes chat_id, content, optional parent_message_id).\n- Gateway: Authenticates session, checks rate limits, and routes to correct - Chat Server using consistent hashing.\n- Validation & Storage: Chat Server verifies user in chat_members. Generates message_id, timestamp, and saves to messages table.\n- Fan-out: Chat Server finds active DeviceSessions and broadcasts new_message to online participants.\n\n2) Rich Media Support (Images/Video)\n- Decoupled Upload: Media is never sent over WebSockets to prevent blocking text messages.\n- Object Storage: Client uploads file directly to an Object Store (e.g., S3) via HTTP REST API.\n- Message Attachment: Client receives a media_url from S3 and attaches it to the standard WebSocket payload.\n\n3) Real-Time Notifications (Online vs. Offline)\n- Presence Check: Chat Server checks device_sessions to split participants into Online and Offline buckets.\n- Online Routing: Broadcasts instantly via WebSocket.\n- Offline Routing: Writes message to inbox table and triggers FCM/APNs push notification.\n- Reconnect Replay: When an offline user opens the app, Gateway connects WS, fetches missed messages from inbox, and marks delivered_at.\n- Cleanup: Background cron job purges undelivered inbox messages after 30 days.\n\n4) Message Deletion\n- Client Request: Client emits delete_message WebSocket event with message_id.\n- Authorization: Chat Server verifies the requester is the original sender_id.\n- Soft Delete: Server updates messages table, setting is_deleted = true (never hard delete).\n- Online Sync: Server broadcasts message_deleted event to instantly update active UIs.\n- Offline Sync (Delivered): Queues deletion event in inbox for devices that already received the text.\n- Offline Sync (Undelivered): Silently removes the inbox row. Recipient never sees the original message or the deletion event.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t2GFgD6fxicVIbnenaMRj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 794.6369317352132,
      "y": 1936.1122062401791,
      "width": 340.7940979003906,
      "height": 35.47869203912893,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bI3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 885837008,
      "version": 1732,
      "versionNonce": 1476477971,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781027472483,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Key Concepts on the go ",
      "fontSize": 28.382953631303145,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Key Concepts on the go ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ZkBBWKb1vT2HifWUbXKkq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 776.6693230263711,
      "y": 1994.2777392044184,
      "width": 732.9198328673299,
      "height": 850,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#eebefa",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bI9",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1874489904,
      "version": 710,
      "versionNonce": 1086776541,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781027621070,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) Preview Thumbnails (Storyboard / Scrubbing)\n- Core Principle: Fetch in batches, not per-hover.\n    > Mechanism: The server groups multiple thumbnail frames into a single\nimage grid called a \"Sprite Sheet\". The client downloads the whole sheet\nat once and uses CSS to crop and display the right frame.\n    > Result: Zero network API calls for every pixel you move your mouse.\n\n- Phase 1: Upload & Processing (Server-Side)\n    > Process: Video is transcoded, frames are extracted (e.g., every 5\nseconds), shrunk down, and packed into a grid. A metadata file (manifest)\nis created mapping timestamps to exact X,Y pixel coordinates on the\nsheet.\n\n- Phase 2: Playback Initialization (Client-Side)\n    > Process: Before the user even hovers, the player loads the map of\nwhere every thumbnail lives.\n\n- Phase 3: Scrubbing Logic (The Hover Event)\n    > Process: Mouse movements are throttled. The cursor position is\nconverted to a video timestamp, looked up in the memory map, and\ndisplayed using CSS.\n\n- Key Optimizations Layered On Top\n    > Throttling/Debouncing: Prevents firing calculation logic for every\nsingle microscopic mouse movement.\n    > Prefetching: Player silently downloads adjacent sprite sheets in\nanticipation of the user dragging further.\nMulti-resolution Storyboards: A low-density, lightweight sheet covering the\nwhole video loads instantly for fast scrubbing, while high-density sheets\nload on demand for fine details.\n    > Pure CSS Cropping: Uses standard CSS background-position to shift\nthe \"window\" over the sprite sheet, requiring zero heavy Javascript image\nrendering.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) Preview Thumbnails (Storyboard / Scrubbing)\n- Core Principle: Fetch in batches, not per-hover.\n    > Mechanism: The server groups multiple thumbnail frames into a single image grid called a \"Sprite Sheet\". The client downloads the whole sheet at once and uses CSS to crop and display the right frame.\n    > Result: Zero network API calls for every pixel you move your mouse.\n\n- Phase 1: Upload & Processing (Server-Side)\n    > Process: Video is transcoded, frames are extracted (e.g., every 5 seconds), shrunk down, and packed into a grid. A metadata file (manifest) is created mapping timestamps to exact X,Y pixel coordinates on the sheet.\n\n- Phase 2: Playback Initialization (Client-Side)\n    > Process: Before the user even hovers, the player loads the map of where every thumbnail lives.\n\n- Phase 3: Scrubbing Logic (The Hover Event)\n    > Process: Mouse movements are throttled. The cursor position is converted to a video timestamp, looked up in the memory map, and displayed using CSS.\n\n- Key Optimizations Layered On Top\n    > Throttling/Debouncing: Prevents firing calculation logic for every single microscopic mouse movement.\n    > Prefetching: Player silently downloads adjacent sprite sheets in anticipation of the user dragging further.\nMulti-resolution Storyboards: A low-density, lightweight sheet covering the whole video loads instantly for fast scrubbing, while high-density sheets load on demand for fine details.\n    > Pure CSS Cropping: Uses standard CSS background-position to shift the \"window\" over the sprite sheet, requiring zero heavy Javascript image rendering.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
